Subject: elf2efi: set MajorImageVersion to 1

GRUB 2.12+ takes the LoadImage()/LoadFile2 path of its EFI "linux" command
only for PE images with MajorImageVersion >= 1 (the Linux EFI stub
convention for "loads its initrd via LoadFile2"). For other images it
falls back to its legacy x86 loader, which exits boot services and enters
the image without its EFI entry point: wimboot cannot run that way.
Needs 0001.

beast-boot (build/wimboot/); to be offered upstream with 0001.

---
--- a/src/elf2efi.c
+++ b/src/elf2efi.c
@@ -291,6 +291,13 @@
 		.OptionalHeader = {
 			.Magic = EFI_IMAGE_NT_OPTIONAL_HDR_MAGIC,
 			.MajorLinkerVersion = 42,
+			/* GRUB's EFI "linux" command starts an image via
+			 * LoadImage() and serves its initrd via LoadFile2
+			 * only for MajorImageVersion >= 1 (the Linux EFI
+			 * stub convention); otherwise it uses its legacy
+			 * loader, which wimboot cannot use.
+			 */
+			.MajorImageVersion = 1,
 			.MinorLinkerVersion = 42,
 			.SectionAlignment = EFI_IMAGE_ALIGN,
 			.FileAlignment = EFI_FILE_ALIGN,
